{"uncertainty": 0.35, "outcome": "Wrote a self-checking SystemVerilog testbench, tick_timer_cov_tb.sv, that extends the approved idle testbench so it exercises every behavior of the approved tick_timer.v. Wrote a coverage report that lists the intended coverage and the constant signals that cannot toggle. No coverage numbers are reported: the platform's coverage.read run over these files has not happened yet.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "coverage_report", "title": "tick_timer coverage closure plan and exclusions", "summary": "Coverage intent for the approved RTL [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.design-under-test.a1], serving [requirement:req-33bb46282b]. It extends the approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.a1]. The baseline run of that testbench, [run:run-0001] ([evidence:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.e1]), passed only 5 checks: reset values and a CTRL readback, with no counting. The new testbench is meant to reach every RTL line and both outcomes of every branch, in this order: (1) Check the reset values. (2) Write LOAD with all ones, then start periodic mode with IE set (CTRL=7). The count is checked to load 0xFFFF and decrement to 0xFFFB. (3) Apply a reset in the middle of the run. This takes the high bits of load and count from 1 back to 0. (4) Run a one-shot of 3. It is checked to expire, set STATUS and irq, clear EN, and hold the count at 0. (5) Write STATUS with bit 0 low: expired must stay set. Write it with bit 0 high: expired and irq must clear. (6) Run periodic mode with a load of 2 and IE=0. The count is checked to reload, set expired, and leave irq low. (7) Write STATUS 1 at the same edge as an expiry: expired must stay set. (8) Write CTRL at the zero-count edge while EN is already set. The expiry must be suppressed, with no reload, and must happen one edge later. (9) Disable the timer: the count must hold. Every bit of wdata, addr, we and rst_n is driven both ways. Signals that cannot toggle, to be justified rather than counted as covered: rdata[31:16] are constant 0 for W=16, by design. unused_wdata is constant 0 by construction (&{1'b0,...}). These must be excluded or waived, not treated as holes or as covered. The case default arm is reached through addr=3 (STATUS reads)."}], "files": [{"path": "tick_timer_cov_tb.sv", "kind": "testbench", "title": "tick_timer coverage testbench", "summary": "Self-checking SystemVerilog testbench for the approved RTL [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.design-under-test.a1], with W=16. It extends the approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.a1] and covers reset, LOAD/CTRL/COUNT/STATUS access, one-shot and periodic expiry, the W1C clear, expiry winning over a clear, and a CTRL write suppressing an expiry. It prints the NIRMAAN-SIM pass/fail line and calls $finish. Traces to [requirement:req-33bb46282b].", "entry": "tick_timer_cov_tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run-0001"], "claims": ["The testbench is expected to pass every check on the approved RTL, based on a manual cycle-by-cycle trace of tick_timer.v. Nothing in the evidence shows this has been run.", "rdata[31:16] and unused_wdata are expected to show no toggles because they are structurally constant for W=16.", "Toggle coverage of count[15:0] and load[15:0] in both directions depends on the mid-test reset after the 0xFFFF load."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Only run-0001, the baseline run of the idle testbench, is cited. The coverage.read run over tick_timer_cov_tb.sv must be done by the platform before review. The coverage bounds themselves (docs/COVERAGE_READ.md) were not given to me, so whether the targets are met is uncertain. The coverage report is an artifact rather than a file, so it is not handed to coverage.read as an HDL source. Independent review of this work is still required (review_record)."}
=== FILE: tick_timer_cov_tb.sv ===
// Coverage testbench for tick_timer.v (W = 16). Extends the approved idle
// testbench: exercises reset, all four registers, one-shot and periodic
// expiry, the W1C clear, expiry-beats-clear, CTRL-write-suppresses-expiry,
// reload, disable and a mid-run reset (for toggle coverage of load/count).
// Structurally constant, justified exclusions: rdata[31:16] (W = 16) and
// dut.unused_wdata (constant 0 by construction).
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module tick_timer_cov_tb;
    localparam logic [1:0] A_CTRL = 2'd0, A_LOAD = 2'd1, A_COUNT = 2'd2, A_STATUS = 2'd3;

    logic        clk = 1'b0;
    logic        rst_n = 1'b0;
    logic        we = 1'b0;
    logic [1:0]  addr = 2'd0;
    logic [31:0] wdata = 32'd0;
    logic [31:0] rdata;
    logic        irq;
    int checks = 0, errors = 0;
    logic [8*64-1:0] nonce;

    tick_timer #(.W(16)) dut (.clk(clk), .rst_n(rst_n), .we(we), .addr(addr), .wdata(wdata), .rdata(rdata), .irq(irq));
    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    task automatic expect_reg(input logic [1:0] a, input logic [31:0] expected, input int tag);
        addr = a;
        #1;
        checks++;
        if (rdata !== expected) begin
            errors++;
            $display("ERROR tag %0d: reg %0d read %h, expected %h at %0t", tag, a, rdata, expected, $time);
        end
    endtask

    task automatic expect_irq(input logic expected, input int tag);
        checks++;
        if (irq !== expected) begin
            errors++;
            $display("ERROR tag %0d: irq %b, expected %b at %0t", tag, irq, expected, $time);
        end
    endtask

    task automatic write(input logic [1:0] a, input logic [31:0] d);
        we = 1'b1; addr = a; wdata = d;
        @(posedge clk); #1;
        we = 1'b0; wdata = 32'd0;
    endtask

    task automatic do_reset;
        we = 1'b0; wdata = 32'd0;
        rst_n = 1'b0;
        repeat (2) @(posedge clk);
        #1;
        rst_n = 1'b1;
    endtask

    task automatic wait_count_zero(input int tag);
        int n;
        n = 0;
        addr = A_COUNT;
        #1;
        while (rdata !== 32'd0 && n < 100) begin
            @(posedge clk); #1;
            n++;
        end
        checks++;
        if (rdata !== 32'd0) begin
            errors++;
            $display("ERROR tag %0d: count never reached zero at %0t", tag, $time);
        end
    endtask

    initial begin
        // 1. Reset values and CTRL read back (as the idle testbench).
        repeat (3) @(posedge clk);
        rst_n = 1'b1;
        @(posedge clk);
        #1;
        expect_reg(A_CTRL, 32'd0, 1);
        expect_reg(A_LOAD, 32'd0, 2);
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd0, 3);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd0, 4);
        expect_irq(1'b0, 5);
        write(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0006);          // EN=0: no start, no reload
        expect_reg(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0006, 6);
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd0, 7);
        write(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0000);
        expect_reg(A_CTRL, 32'd0, 8);

        // 2. All-ones LOAD (upper wdata bits ignored), periodic start, countdown.
        write(A_LOAD, 32'hFFFF_FFFF);
        expect_reg(A_LOAD, 32'h0000_FFFF, 10);
        write(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0007);
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'h0000_FFFF, 11);
        expect_reg(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0007, 12);
        repeat (4) @(posedge clk);
        #1;
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'h0000_FFFB, 13);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd0, 14);
        expect_irq(1'b0, 15);

        // 3. Mid-run reset: everything back to zero.
        do_reset;
        expect_reg(A_CTRL, 32'd0, 20);
        expect_reg(A_LOAD, 32'd0, 21);
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd0, 22);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd0, 23);
        expect_irq(1'b0, 24);

        // 4. One-shot of 3 with IE: expires, sets STATUS and irq, clears EN.
        write(A_LOAD, 32'd3);
        write(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0005);
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd3, 30);
        expect_reg(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0005, 31);
        @(posedge clk); #1;
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd2, 32);
        repeat (3) @(posedge clk);
        #1;
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd1, 33);
        expect_irq(1'b1, 34);
        expect_reg(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0004, 35);
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd0, 36);
        repeat (2) @(posedge clk);
        #1;
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd0, 37);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd1, 38);

        // 5. W1C: writing bit 0 low keeps EXPIRED, writing a one clears it.
        write(A_STATUS, 32'hFFFF_FFFE);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd1, 40);
        expect_irq(1'b1, 41);
        write(A_STATUS, 32'h0000_0001);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd0, 42);
        expect_irq(1'b0, 43);

        // 6. Periodic of 2 without IE: reload on expiry, irq stays low.
        write(A_LOAD, 32'd2);
        write(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0003);
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd2, 50);
        repeat (3) @(posedge clk);
        #1;
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd2, 51);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd1, 52);
        expect_reg(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0003, 53);
        expect_irq(1'b0, 54);
        @(posedge clk); #1;
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd1, 55);

        // 7. An expiry wins over a clear at the same edge.
        write(A_STATUS, 32'h0000_0001);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd0, 60);
        wait_count_zero(61);
        write(A_STATUS, 32'h0000_0001);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd1, 62);
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd2, 63);

        // 8. A CTRL write at the zero edge suppresses the expiry (EN already set: no reload).
        write(A_STATUS, 32'h0000_0001);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd0, 70);
        wait_count_zero(71);
        write(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0003);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd0, 72);
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd0, 73);
        @(posedge clk); #1;
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd1, 74);
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd2, 75);

        // 9. Disable: the count holds.
        write(A_CTRL, 32'h0000_0000);
        expect_reg(A_CTRL, 32'd0, 80);
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd2, 81);
        repeat (3) @(posedge clk);
        #1;
        expect_reg(A_COUNT, 32'd2, 82);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd1, 83);
        expect_irq(1'b0, 84);
        write(A_STATUS, 32'h0000_0001);
        expect_reg(A_STATUS, 32'd0, 85);

        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) nonce = "none";
        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, (checks > errors ? checks - errors : 0), errors);
        $finish;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===
